WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.545
Human imagination.

2
00:00:02.845 --> 00:00:04.885
Adaptive intelligence.

3
00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:13.675
Quesar by MLAI introduces assistant workflows, memory systems and developer tools with inspectable sources.

4
00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:22.142
A place to begin.

5
00:00:22.442 --> 00:00:24.407
Read the architecture.

6
00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:31.947
The website brings products, platform, developers, research, services and contact into one navigation.

7
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.190
Three roles.

8
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.405
One conversation.

9
00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:46.195
Abbey is a human-facing companion contract.

10
00:00:46.495 --> 00:00:49.185
Aviva is a direct expert mode.

11
00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:54.000
Abi coordinates intent, risk, context and response style.

12
00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:02.017
Abbey.

13
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:04.257
Care in the interface.

14
00:01:04.557 --> 00:01:10.247
Thoughtful teaching, creative work and technical collaboration are the intended role.

15
00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:14.937
Actual assistant behavior depends on its configured backend.

16
00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:23.079
Aviva.

17
00:01:23.379 --> 00:01:25.319
Clarity with boundaries.

18
00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:31.634
Concrete next actions and explicit uncertainty define the local persona profile.

19
00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:35.599
A role alone does not establish model quality.

20
00:01:42.252 --> 00:01:43.617
Abi.

21
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:46.282
Coordination, inspected.

22
00:01:46.582 --> 00:01:51.922
Local routing and scheduler helpers select a persona or controlled blend.

23
00:01:52.222 --> 00:01:54.887
Broader governance remains partial.

24
00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:03.004
Memory.

25
00:02:03.304 --> 00:02:05.019
Keep its provenance.

26
00:02:05.319 --> 00:02:13.684
WDBX local Rust storage and retrieval components preserve durable records, vectors and causal history.

27
00:02:20.336 --> 00:02:21.951
Integrity.

28
00:02:22.251 --> 00:02:24.241
Truth needs evidence.

29
00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:27.981
Storage integrity does not make a statement true.

30
00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:34.596
Production multi-host WDBX deployment is not established by this website.

31
00:02:41.249 --> 00:02:42.914
Developers.

32
00:02:43.214 --> 00:02:44.879
Start with source.

33
00:02:45.179 --> 00:02:50.644
Explore the ABI Rust framework, local CLI and MCP contracts.

34
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:56.309
Follow setup and verification guidance before connecting tools or memory.

35
00:03:02.961 --> 00:03:04.651
APIs.

36
00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.841
State availability.

37
00:03:07.141 --> 00:03:12.106
Hosted Quesar APIs and platform SDKs are not published.

38
00:03:12.406 --> 00:03:15.921
The website points to local frameworks and contracts.

39
00:03:22.573 --> 00:03:24.113
Two names.

40
00:03:24.413 --> 00:03:26.228
Two distinct scopes.

41
00:03:26.528 --> 00:03:30.668
Quesar is the MLAI website and broader direction.

42
00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:35.808
Quasar is the separately configured local website builder service.

43
00:03:42.461 --> 00:03:44.001
Quasar.

44
00:03:44.301 --> 00:03:46.316
Browser to your service.

45
00:03:46.616 --> 00:03:51.456
The Quasar screens call the configured service directly from the browser.

46
00:03:51.756 --> 00:03:54.546
This website does not spawn that service.

47
00:04:01.198 --> 00:04:02.613
Connect.

48
00:04:02.913 --> 00:04:04.728
Choose an origin.

49
00:04:05.028 --> 00:04:09.843
Settings lets the browser reach a local service and check that it answers.

50
00:04:10.143 --> 00:04:13.458
The deployment may supply a default origin.

51
00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.550
Pairing.

52
00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.815
A deliberate connection.

53
00:04:24.115 --> 00:04:27.205
The settings screen includes a pairing token.

54
00:04:27.505 --> 00:04:32.870
Saving a connection and revoking an online pairing are explicit operations.

55
00:04:39.523 --> 00:04:41.163
A new site.

56
00:04:41.463 --> 00:04:43.253
Begin with a prompt.

57
00:04:43.553 --> 00:04:53.768
The local service copies a Next.js template into its sites directory and runs a Claude generation job using that machine’s Anthropic credentials.

58
00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.360
A local library.

59
00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.450
Read live sites.

60
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:11.315
The sites screen reads generated sites from the configured local service, directly through the browser.

61
00:05:17.967 --> 00:05:19.657
Generation.

62
00:05:19.957 --> 00:05:21.672
Follow the feed.

63
00:05:21.972 --> 00:05:27.012
The site detail screen polls service feed and preview state every second.

64
00:05:27.312 --> 00:05:32.102
A generation is a job to inspect, not an invisible promise.

65
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:40.320
Refinement.

66
00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.560
Send a change request.

67
00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.275
The site detail screen offers an edit prompt.

68
00:05:46.575 --> 00:05:51.765
The route follows generation, sends edits and previews the site on your machine.

69
00:05:58.417 --> 00:05:59.907
Preview.

70
00:06:00.207 --> 00:06:02.047
A separate opening.

71
00:06:02.347 --> 00:06:09.262
Preview launch obtains a ticket and checks the returned target against the configured service before opening it.

72
00:06:15.914 --> 00:06:17.479
Recovery.

73
00:06:17.779 --> 00:06:19.969
Uncertainty is visible.

74
00:06:20.269 --> 00:06:29.784
The connection API exposes uncertain mutation state and recovery so screens can offer Retry rather than silently assuming success.

75
00:06:36.437 --> 00:06:37.977
Research.

76
00:06:38.277 --> 00:06:40.567
Ideas beside evidence.

77
00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:49.032
Source-backed work covers memory, retrieval, orchestration and provenance, with implementation status beside the research.

78
00:06:55.684 --> 00:06:57.174
NYON.

79
00:06:57.474 --> 00:06:59.464
Deterministic worlds.

80
00:06:59.764 --> 00:07:06.179
NYON is a related Rust strategy game with a separate offline Galaxy Workshop sandbox.

81
00:07:06.479 --> 00:07:10.694
Desktop and browser qualification remain in progress.

82
00:07:17.346 --> 00:07:19.261
The open workshop.

83
00:07:19.561 --> 00:07:21.451
Build with the source.

84
00:07:21.751 --> 00:07:30.191
Public repositories, documentation and plugins invite exploration through each project’s own contribution workflow.

85
00:07:36.844 --> 00:07:38.684
The future studio.

86
00:07:38.984 --> 00:07:41.049
Visual orchestration.

87
00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:51.264
MLAI Studio is a proposed workspace for visual agent design, prompt experiments and inspecting context, memory and execution.

88
00:07:57.916 --> 00:07:59.831
Many modalities.

89
00:08:00.131 --> 00:08:02.046
Explicit boundaries.

90
00:08:02.346 --> 00:08:11.311
Text, images, audio, code and spatial environments are a direction for future collaboration with explicit data boundaries.

91
00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:19.803
MLAI Network.

92
00:08:20.103 --> 00:08:22.118
A proposed community.

93
00:08:22.418 --> 00:08:28.683
The future network would let builders share agents, plugins, research, projects and extensions.

94
00:08:28.983 --> 00:08:30.998
It remains proposed.

95
00:08:37.651 --> 00:08:39.516
Static and server.

96
00:08:39.816 --> 00:08:41.706
Different capabilities.

97
00:08:42.006 --> 00:08:46.071
The static website renders notices for server features.

98
00:08:46.371 --> 00:08:51.211
A configured server deployment is needed for server-backed capabilities.

99
00:08:57.863 --> 00:08:59.953
Model configuration.

100
00:09:00.253 --> 00:09:02.193
Honest availability.

101
00:09:02.493 --> 00:09:05.408
The site uses one model interface.

102
00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:12.623
When no provider is configured, its model state is not configured rather than an invented response.

103
00:09:19.275 --> 00:09:20.890
Services.

104
00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.105
Define the evidence.

105
00:09:23.405 --> 00:09:28.145
Explore the services and contact pages to discuss a project.

106
00:09:28.445 --> 00:09:33.060
Scope, verification and operational boundaries should be explicit.

107
00:09:39.713 --> 00:09:41.503
Build thoughtfully.

108
00:09:41.803 --> 00:09:43.743
quesar.cloud

109
00:09:44.043 --> 00:09:46.183
Explore the architecture.

110
00:09:46.483 --> 00:09:48.248
Follow the source.

111
00:09:48.548 --> 00:09:51.388
Define the evidence your project needs.

112
00:09:51.688 --> 00:09:53.878
Quesar by MLAI.
